2026-08-25T00:00:00Z (RFD66606-1059) 'Continuous integration, in one step
 # uuid: 6031ae2f-d700-5c6e-9ed3-2949de72ddc8
 # tags: rfd:title, rfd:attest-in:none
 RFD:Published  1 RFD
 Serials:Weftspun

2026-08-25T00:00:01Z (RFD66606-1059) '`scripts/ci.sh`, `.github/workflows/main.yml`
 # tags: rfd:scope, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD1059  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-1059) 'One command builds and self-tests the whole system before every commit.
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD1059  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-1059) '`.github/workflows/main.yml` ran `npm run test:anim-regression`. `package.json` never defined that script.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD1059  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-1059) 'Run `scripts/ci.sh` before committing, and read below for the three steps in order.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD1059  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-1059) 'Continuous integration, in one step
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD1059  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-1059) 'Follow Martin Fowler's ["Continuous Integration"](https://martinfowler.com/articles/continuousIntegration.html). One command builds and self-tests the whole system. A developer runs it before committing, and the integration machine runs the identical command.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD1059  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-1059) '`scripts/ci.sh` is that one command. A developer runs it before committing, and an integration machine runs the identical command.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD1059  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-1059) 'RFD66606-1058 gives the two container images this script builds. RFD66606-1020 gives the CockroachDB the Elixir step tests against.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD1059  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-1059) 'Fowler's two practices
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1059  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-1059) 'Two of his practices name the fault directly. "Automate the Build" and "Make Your Build Self-Testing" are the two. A broken `npm run` line that only ran on GitHub's machine shows what happens when the person who last touched a build never runs it.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1059  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-1059) 'What the one step does
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1059  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-1059) 'In order, stopping at the first failure:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1059  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-1059) '1. `npm install`, `vitest run`, `npm run build`. The JS side.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1059  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-1059) '2. `mix deps.get`, `mix compile --warnings-as-errors`, `mix test` against an ephemeral CockroachDB node the script starts and tears down itself (`mix weftspun.crdb`). The Elixir side.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1059  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-1059) '3. `podman build` (or `docker build`, whichever is on `PATH`) for both RFD66606-1058 images. No push, build only.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1059  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-1059) 'Each step must pass before the next runs. A JS test failure never reaches the Elixir suite. A compile warning fails the build the same as a test failure does, per `--warnings-as-errors`.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1059  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-1059) 'Why one script, not three CI steps
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1059  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-1059) 'A step written only in YAML runs nowhere but GitHub's machine. This repository's one broken CI step proves what that costs. Nobody ran it locally, so nobody noticed it never worked. A shell script runs on a laptop and on a runner identically, through `bash scripts/ci.sh`, so the gap this RFD closes cannot reopen the same way.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1059  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-1059) '`CONTAINER_ENGINE` picks `podman` first, falling back to `docker`, because this project develops against Podman (RFD66606-1058), while GitHub's runners ship Docker. The Dockerfiles are engine-agnostic. Neither one assumes Podman.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1059  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-1059) 'Retracted for now: the GitHub workflow that called the script
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1059  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-1059) '`.github/workflows/main.yml` once installed the toolchains and called `scripts/ci.sh`, and nothing in it duplicated a step the script already ran. That file is deleted, on purpose.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1059  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-1059) '`scripts/ci.sh` still exists, still runs the same one command, and a developer still runs it before committing. The browser client's own test suite carries many pre-existing failures across several files, unrelated to any one commit, and every push turned red for that reason alone. RFD66606-1057 tracks restoring the workflow once that suite is fixed.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1059  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-1059) 'The decision this retracts is Fowler's, not this repository's, and it still holds. One command builds and self-tests the system. What is missing is the machine that runs it, not the command.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1059  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-1059) 'What this does not cover
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1059  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-1059) 'Playwright (`test:e2e`) and the smoke scripts under `test:anim-smoke` / `test:appearance-*` stay outside `scripts/ci.sh`. They need a browser, or a running dev server this RFD does not stand up.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1059  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-1059) 'RFD66606-1058's `deploy-weftspun-quadlet.sh` stays outside it too. Continuous integration is not continuous deployment, and RFD66606-1058's open firewall question means that script cannot pass on this host yet regardless.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1059  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-1059) 'The problem
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1059  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:28Z (RFD66606-1059) 'Every run of this job failed at that line. CI stayed red, or silently skipped, since whenever that step was added.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1059  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:29Z (RFD66606-1059) 'It also tested one of three parts of this repository. `weftspun_studio/` had no CI at all, and neither did the two Podman images RFD66606-1058 adds.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1059  1 LINE
 Text:Written
